<p>These yellow rings are not superimposed on an existing photograph &#8212; they&#8217;re actually painted on the landscape. Swiss artist Felice Varini created <em>Three Ellipses for Three Locks</em> in 2014 by painting segments on roads, walls, and nearly 100 buildings in the historic center of Hasselt, Belgium. The effect was visible only to a viewer in one particular vantage point.</p>
